🔗 2. APIs in AI

API = **Application Programming Interface**

👉 It allows communication between applications.

---

🔹 What is an API?

```text id="m7p3yt"
Send request → Get response from model/server
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🌐 Hugging Face Inference API

Allows you to **use models without downloading them**.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Example: Using API

```python id="y5n8vk"
import requests

API_URL = "https://api-inference.huggingface.co/models/distilbert-base-uncased"
headers = {"Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_API_KEY"}

data = {"inputs": "AI is amazing"}

response = requests.post(API_URL, headers=headers, json=data)

print(response.json())
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔐 API Key

You need an API key from Hugging Face:

* Create account
* Generate token
* Use in headers

---

⚡ Advantages of APIs

✔ No need for local setup
✔ Fast integration
✔ Scalable
✔ Easy deployment

---

⚠️ Limitations

❌ Requires internet
❌ Rate limits
❌ API cost (in some cases)

---

🔄 Workflow

```text id="u3z7kp"
Load Dataset → Train/Use Model → Use API → Build Application
```

